          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What form does शक्नोति (śaknoti) take as its object? (The -तुम् form.) Say \"the boy can go\"."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SA-C57-icchati",
      "sequence": 2730,
      "title": "इच्छति (icchati) — wants",
      "headword": "इच्छति",
      "romanization": "icchati",
      "gloss": "wants — the same frame as शक्नोति, with wanting in place of being able",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:03a5d4a6aee82c5c",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say \"the boy can go\". Which of the two words in it is the -तुम् form?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: इच्छति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इच्छति (icchati) — \"wants, wishes\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is nothing new to learn about the frame. It is the frame you built one lesson ago, with a different verb at the end of it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बालः पठितुम् इच्छति bālaḥ paṭhitum icchati the boy wants to read."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Compare the pair and the shape holds still while the meaning turns:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "sentence",
                "meaning"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "बालः पठितुम् शक्नोति (śaknoti) means the boy can read.",
                "बालः पठितुम् इच्छति (icchati) means the boy wants to read."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is what makes the -तुम् form worth the lesson it got two chapters back. It is not one construction; it is a socket, and ability and desire are the first two things to plug into it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The root is इष्, \"to seek\" — and the noun it makes is one you may have met in English writing about India: इच्छा (icchā), \"wish, desire\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Desire, in the frame you already had."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
